Author: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date:   Wed Oct 14 23:26:18 2026 +0000

    feat(sandbox-agent): boot a container with systemd as PID 1

    A container sandbox's entrypoint is now its init, as every other sandbox's
    is (ADR 26-10-10-767). The `init` subcommand and its exec plan are gone;
    discobox-wire.service runs `discobox-sandbox-agent wire` (boot.Wire)
    instead. It provisions the user from the bootstrap, binds the config and
    secrets volumes, wires the declared volumes and the sources, writes the
    units bound to the sandbox user and reloads the manager.

    The unit is ordered before local-fs.target and required by
    sysinit.target, so every unit that uses a wired path starts after it, and
    after tmp.mount and systemd-sysusers.service. It runs only where the
    config volume is, and on every boot. A failure exits the container with
    status 1 (FailureAction=exit-force), logging to the console, so the pool
    reports it instead of a sandbox writing its state into the image layer.

    The secrets bind moves out of the agent's server process into the unit,
    which already runs after systemd's /run tmpfs is mounted. Provision, the
    VM path, shares the unit reload and is otherwise unchanged. The boxd twin
    installs and enables the unit, which a machine skips.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

